WEBVTT

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.860
It's so hot.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:23.000
<b>#13  We're In Taiwan!!</b>

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.000
It feels way more like 
summer here than in Japan.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.010
Taiwan, huh?

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.480
Taiwan?

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:08.830
Yes. We're actually discussing 
the possibility of going

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:11.360
to Taiwan for next year's school trip.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:12.820
Taiwan?

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.050
They've been friendly 
with Japan for a long time.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.000
They're apparently very welcoming 
toward Japanese people.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.930
Their comics culture is well-developed, too.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:25.640
I went to Kyoto and Nara on school trips 
in middle school, so Taiwan sounds good.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:26.580
Ahem.

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:34.300
How is that related to why you asked 
the bicycle club to come here?

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:38.300
Did you know Taiwan is 
a major producer of bicycles?

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.750
Korone might have mentioned that.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:46.210
The exhibition she went to 
was in Taiwan, wasn't it?

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.640
The bike I ride was made in Taiwan, too.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:53.540
Its bicycle production isn't 
the only thing that's amazing.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.500
People use bicycles for transportation 
 in Taiwan more than they do in Japan.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.360
There are even systems established 
that allow you to easily rent a bike.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.670
You can rent bikes in Kamakura, too.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.770
Their system is a little different.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.460
Different how?

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.620
I want you to go see for yourselves.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:14.700
In other words, you mean...

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:18.260
You want us to conduct a preliminary 
inspection for the school trip?

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.910
That's right. We'll cover the costs.

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:23.090
While you're gone, you'll be treated 
as if you were on vacation.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.970
Naturally, you'll need to submit a report.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.890
But what do you think?
Would you like to go to Taiwan?

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.280
Of course.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.610
We'll go!

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.290
Sensei, I don't see our guide anywhere.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:41.250
That's not good.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.870
She were supposed to meet us at the airport.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:49.770
Speaking of which, I don't 
see Hiromi or Sandy, either.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:50.660
What?

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.250
When did they disappear?

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.120
Let's start exploring Taiwan!

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:56.130
Yay!

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.050
Look, Sandy. They're selling souvenirs.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:06.410
Maybe I'll buy something for my mom.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.250
No, no, Hiromi.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:12.940
You should buy souvenirs just before you leave,
 or your luggage will be too heavy.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.360
You're so smart, Sandy.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.190
Natsumi-chan!

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.410
Shénme?

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:20.440
Natsumi, are you adventuring, too?

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.390
Come with us.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.060
E-Excuse me...

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:24.820
What?

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.780
I think you have the wrong person.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:28.910
Huh?

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.150
What?

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:41.180
The more I look, the more they seem alike.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.970
It's like you're twins.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:47.560
If you switched clothes, I wouldn't be 
able to tell which one is you.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:52.180
Not only that, but it's even more 
 surprising that she's our guide.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:55.320
Sorry I'm late. I got 
caught up in some traffic.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.580
<b>Welcome
 Minami Kamakura Girls Bicycle Club
And Party</b>

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:59.770
My name is Su Jinwan. Please call me Su.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.930
So this is a Taiwanese city, huh?

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:11.200
All the signs full of 
kanji feel so Taiwanese.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:14.830
But they have some of the
 same convenience stores as Japan.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.040
It's kind of strange.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.400
It's not just convenience stores.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:23.720
We even have some of the same cafés and 
fast food restaurants you have in Japan.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:25.630
Really?

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.550
Anyway, Su, your Japanese is really good.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:32.950
Thanks. I attended college in Tokyo.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.430
Oh, really?

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.190
No wonder you're fluent in Japanese.

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:39.530
Not just Japanese.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:43.500
Right now, I'm studying 
English, Spanish, and French.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.640
What? That many languages?

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:50.370
Yeah. It's my dream to travel
 around the world someday.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.470
The whole world?

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:53.240
Wow!

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:57.620
I have no idea when that will happen, though.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.500
Is this all of your luggage?

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.800
Yes. There are also some packages 
we had shipped from Japan.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.010
Your bicycles, right?

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:15.060
They made it here safely.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:19.980
Now that you've dropped off
 your bags, let's get some lunch.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.300
All right!

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:22.940
I'm hungry.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.900
Wow.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:32.480
Since this is your first meal, I thought 
we could have traditional Taiwanese food.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.070
Bon appétit.

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:35.870
Thanks for the food!

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:41.210
It's so good.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:46.930
Hey, Su. What's that?

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:49.800
That's YouBike.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.470
YouBike?

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:55.010
It must be the bike rental 
service the principal mentioned.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:57.610
Can anyone rent a bike?

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:59.180
Would you like to check it out later?

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.940
What cute bikes.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:06.380
They have baskets on them
 like Japanese mommy bikes.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:08.860
How do you rent a bike?

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.490
It's simple.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:16.200
Use your card to release the lock, 
and you've rented a bike.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.160
Wow, it really is simple.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.670
Do we bring them back here to return them?

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.310
Here is fine,

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:29.550
but you can return your bike to any of 
the roughly 200 stations around Taipei.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.950
Any one of 200 stations?

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.930
It certainly is quite a bit different 
from the bike rental places

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.970
you see around Japan.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:45.610
<b>Public Bicycle Station</b>

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:40.300
Hey, couldn't we use 
these on our school trip?

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:43.480
Yeah, we could go sightseeing 
around Taipei on bikes.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.610
That sounds fun.

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:46.870
What do you think?

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:50.940
It's a bit early to check into the hotel,
so would you like to give YouBike a try?

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:52.290
Yeah!

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:58.370
On Taiwanese bikes, your left 
hand controls your front brake,

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:02.830
and your right hand controls 
your rear brake, so be careful.

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:06.400
So they're the opposite of Japanese bikes.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:08.090
This feels kind of weird.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.760
Is everyone ready?

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:11.810
Yes.

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:14.020
Then let's go sightseeing.

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:15.820
Let's go!

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:53.800
True to its name, the Taipei 101 has
101 stories and is 509.2 meters tall.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:58.100
When it was completed, it was the 
tallest building in the world.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.050
Really?

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:03.200
Look, Hiromi. The people look like ants.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:04.270
Really?

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:07.650
They look smaller than ants 
or even grains of rice.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:10.320
I'm surprised you can go 
all the way to the edge.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.110
Huh? Fuyune-chan, are you scared?

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:15.440
O-Of course not.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:17.730
Then come over here and 
check out the view with us.

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:19.100
Yeah.

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.700
What? Hey, wait...

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:22.580
Here you go.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.130
Sorry, Fuyune-chan.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:35.090
I didn't know you were afraid of heights.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:37.800
You should've told us.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:40.140
I-I never said that.

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:42.650
I'm totally fine.

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:45.260
Let's head to our next stop.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:20.510
Wow, there are so many people.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:21.870
The air's so hot.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.220
It really feels like Asia here.

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:27.980
This is one of Taiwan's iconic
night spots, the night market.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.670
Hiromi, are you hungry?

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:31.710
Of course.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.260
Do you have money?

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:34.300
Of course.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:35.110
Then...

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:37.000
Let's go!

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.920
There they go again.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:40.790
Let's follow them.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:41.610
Yeah.

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:44.370
Wait. You girls, too?

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:49.290
I guess there's no point 
in trying to stop them.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.250
We should enjoy ourselves.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:51.960
Yes.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.040
Wh-What is this?

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.760
It looks like tofu.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:12.400
What is this smell? Is it rotten?

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:15.810
It's called stinky tofu.

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.830
It's a dish made of fermented tofu.

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:20.150
It's very popular in Taiwan.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.120
Huh?

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:31.560
The smell doesn't bother you 
that much when you eat it.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:34.390
It's different from Okinawan tofuyo, but...

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:36.650
This isn't too bad.

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:38.590
This is actually pretty good.

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:40.420
Do you like it?

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.470
Yes, very much.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:49.670
Excuse me.

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:50.390
What?

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:53.690
Are there any good Taiwanese 
foods around here?

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:55.940
Oh, uh...

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:56.900
Sure.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:59.960
There is a perfect choice for you over there.

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:01.320
Please follow me.

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:03.870
Nice job, Su.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.540
She's so cool.

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:08.730
Thank you.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:10.160
Careful. It's hot.

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:18.210
I hope you had fun today.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:21.520
I'll come to get you at 
8:00 tomorrow morning.

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:23.430
Get some rest until then.

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.570
Shall we head to our room?

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:30.250
Sorry, but I've got someplace to go.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:31.820
You girls head to bed.

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:34.040
Where are you going at this hour?

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:36.770
That's not for kids to know.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:38.230
What?

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:41.150
I'm just kidding.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:43.810
Taiwan's famous for its foot massages.

00:12:43.810 --> 00:12:48.240
I'm going to release all the exhaustion 
I've built up from working all day.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:49.010
Oh.

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:50.450
You're just going for a massage.

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:54.130
Thank you.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:55.000
Okay.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:10.010
Sensei, how was your massage?

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:12.900
I feel great now.

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:16.480
<i>I didn't think it would 
be that painful, though.</i>

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:22.280
Good morning, everyone.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.570
Put your bikes in here.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.350
Huh? What's this?

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:28.990
That's my road bike.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.500
Su, you ride bikes, too?

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:34.960
Yes. Today I'll be joining you.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.560
Su is amazing. She can do anything.

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:40.010
Yeah...

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:48.830
Hey, Su. The place we're 
going today is a lake, right?

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:53.040
That's right. It's a freshwater lake
 in the mountains, 749 meters above sea level

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.430
called Sun Moon Lake.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:14:00.420
<b>Sun Moon Lake</b>

00:13:54.430 --> 00:14:00.420
It's called the Sun Moon Lake because 
it's shaped like the sun and the moon.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.530
It was chosen as one of 
the Eight Wonders of Taiwan,

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.740
and it's also Taiwan's largest lake.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:08.390
What? The largest lake in Taiwan?

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:11.320
We're going to bike around that?

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:13.040
Don't worry.

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:16.780
It may be the largest, but it's 
still only thirty-nine kilometers around.

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:18.620
Oh, good.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.220
Let's go.

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:51.770
I thought the trail would be
 flatter around a lake.

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:53.830
There's a lot of ups and downs.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:57.580
And we can't see the lake at all.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.150
Keep at it, everyone.

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:01.750
We're almost there.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:07.590
Wow, it's beautiful.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.330
No wonder it's one of the Eight Wonders.

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:12.550
It was worth climbing up those hills.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:17.020
<b>Home of Taiwanese
Black Tea</b>

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:14.600
Taipei was nice,

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:18.980
but I think cycling around here on 
the school trip could be good, too.

00:15:21.210 --> 00:15:21.830
Here.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.390
We'd better re-hydrate.

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:26.670
Thanks.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:35.600
<b>Home of Taiwanese
Black Tea</b>

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:32.210
Did something happen, Natsumi-chan?

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:34.170
You seem down.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:39.020
Look. Su's talking to some strangers again.

00:15:39.020 --> 00:15:40.290
You're right.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:43.330
Su gets along with everyone.

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.590
I'm jealous.

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:46.290
Huh?

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:51.560
I want to travel around the
 world someday, like Su does.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:55.300
What? Natsumi-chan, that's amazing.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:16:00.480
But I don't think I can do it.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:01.930
Why not?

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:06.590
I can't get along with strangers like Su can.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:10.650
This is my first time 
traveling overseas, too.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:13.410
I've never even thought 
about studying abroad.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:17.980
When I think about how may we look alike, 
but we're totally different inside,

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:18.920
I just...

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:23.110
How can I be like her?

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:24.830
That's all you're worried about?

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:25.670
What?

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:29.050
Just ask her.

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:36.320
Take your time.

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:40.490
Uh, sorry about that.

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:43.340
Hiromi is pretty forceful, isn't she?

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:44.480
Yes.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.150
I'm jealous.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.000
What?

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:51.030
I'm not as proactive as her.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.670
Th-That's not true.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:56.120
You went to college in Japan,

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:59.120
and you're studying various languages 
to make your dream a reality.

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:04.330
I'd never left Taiwan 
until I went to college.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:08.880
You're far more proactive than me for 
coming to Taiwan as high school students.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:09.900
But...

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:13.240
I was introverted in high school.

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:16.850
I was nervous around strangers 
and couldn't talk to them.

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:18.360
What? You?

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:18.890
Yeah.

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:23.020
But one day, I realized

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:26.680
the people I was meeting for the 
first time must be nervous, too.

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:31.480
So if I don't take the first step 
toward them, we'll never be friends.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:36.360
I was nervous when I met all of you yesterday,

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:40.250
but I'm glad you were there.

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:40.830
What?

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:45.780
I never dreamed someone who 
looked like me would be coming.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:50.500
When I saw your face, my anxiety disappeared.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:53.880
Come to think of it, I didn't 
have time to be nervous, either.

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:56.140
You can take it slow.

00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:59.090
Go at your own pace and 
take it one step at a time.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:02.200
The world's not going anywhere.

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:05.270
Slowly, at my own pace...

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:09.890
I'm still on my way up.

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:15.240
My ultimate goal is to tour around 
Europe on my bike someday.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.080
You want to bike across Europe?

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:19.740
I'm preparing for that right now.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:24.640
That's why I'm studying foreign languages 
and working to save up money.

